# tools/s/standing_equipment_witness.rish -- the roster of standing guards is a list, not a sentence.
#
# WHY THIS RUNG. The standing-equipment roster lived in one paragraph of construction/ITINERARY.md. A
# paragraph can be read and it can be believed; it cannot be run, counted, or dated. The tree paid
# for that twice in two consecutive rounds. REDS %147 found eight standing witnesses each holding a
# count its source had moved past. REDS %149 found the living-pin bound guard unrun for four laps
# while construction/REDS.md sat 2,050 bytes over the bound that guard exists to hold. Each was caught by a
# hand that happened to run something, which is the definition of a lantern rather than a loom.
#
# The grain already seats the sibling strand: a guard that cannot red guards nothing (REDS row 59).
# Two rounds have now taught the strand beside it -- a guard that is never run guards nothing
# either -- so the roster becomes a file a program reads, and the running of it leaves a record.
#
# WHAT IS PROVEN, on metal.
#   Every `path` in construction/standing-equipment.kyri names a file that exists on disk, so the roster
#   can never name equipment the tree has moved or renamed away from underneath it.
#   Every `guard` record carries exactly one `path`, so a half-written row is refused rather than
#   silently skipped by a runner reading the same file.
#   Every `tier` names a cadence the runner honors -- `lap` or `cadence`, with an absent field
#   meaning `lap`. A guard seated on a tier no runner knows would run on no lap at all, in silence,
#   which is REDS %219 wearing a field name.
#   Every `ran` line in the run card names a guard the roster actually seats.
#   No run-card line records a red or an absent guard.
#   Forty-three behaviors are proven on throwaway rosters in a temporary pen -- ten refusals
#   bitten, and the runner itself driven over a planted roster with a stub interpreter, since a
#   tier is only a cadence if the program that reads it actually selects by it. Sixteen of the
#   forty-three run inside a real git repository the control creates and throws away, because two
#   of the runner's refusals are about the repository rather than the roster. Seven are the tree
#   digest: a stub guard that writes nothing leaves it still, one that writes a file moves it.
#   Nine are the unclosed lap: a clean cold open runs its guard, one staged path refuses the same
#   pass before any guard starts, `--hot` passes that same tree, a guard asked for by name runs
#   free over it, and `--hot --all` still selects every tier.
#
#   A full-roster pass opening on a dirty index means a lap ended at `git add`, which left this
#   tree's generated pages stale three times (REDS %188, %220, %223). The runner refuses it under
#   `run_verdict=lap_unclosed`. The refusal is proven beside the case it must NOT bite, since a
#   guard that always refuses cannot be told from one that reads the index at all.
#
# WHAT IS REPORTED RATHER THAN GATED. How many rostered guards have never run on this pier -- in
# total and for the cadence tier alone, which is where a guard can go quiet without anyone
# noticing -- and the oldest recorded run. A fresh clone has genuinely run nothing, so `never run here` is an
# honest reading rather than a defect, and gating it would red every clone on the day it lands.
# The number is printed because a lap can act on a number it can see; the roster in prose offered
# no number at all.
#
# WHAT IS NOT PROVEN. That the roster is COMPLETE -- a guard nobody adds here is a guard this rung
# says nothing about. Completeness is a judgment, and this proves the mechanical half beneath it.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/s/standing_equipment_witness.rish
#
# To refresh the run card, which is untracked by design:
#   sh tools/fixtures/standing_equipment_run.sh              # cold open -- the every-lap tier
#   sh tools/fixtures/standing_equipment_run.sh --hot        # after `git add` -- staged paths are mine
#   sh tools/fixtures/standing_equipment_run.sh --all        # every tier, choirs included

say "standing-equipment: Language EN -- the roster of what guards this tree stood in a paragraph, so nothing could run it, count it, or say when each guard last answered."
say "standing-equipment: Style Radiant -- the roster is a file now, every path in it is real, and running it leaves a record on disk rather than in the memory of a round."
say "standing-equipment: Lens TAME -- safety first: a guard that cannot red guards nothing, and a guard that is never run guards nothing either."

let scan = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/standing_equipment_scan.sh"]
assert scan.ok else "standing-equipment: the roster names something the tree cannot honor -- read the scan's own lines"
say scan.out
assert scan.out contains "guards_path_missing=0" else "standing-equipment: every rostered path must name a file that exists"
assert scan.out contains "guards_half_written=0" else "standing-equipment: every guard record must carry exactly one path"
assert scan.out contains "guards_unknown_tier=0" else "standing-equipment: every tier must name a cadence the runner honors"
assert scan.out contains "runs_unrostered=0" else "standing-equipment: a run card may only name guards the roster seats"
assert scan.out contains "runs_red=0" else "standing-equipment: a recorded red is a stopped line, never a passing roster"
assert scan.out contains "verdict=ok" else "standing-equipment: the scan must balance before it is believed"
say "field GREEN -- every rostered guard names a real file, and no recorded run is red"

let control = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/standing_equipment_control.sh"]
assert control.ok else "standing-equipment: the control must complete"
say control.out
assert control.out contains "agreeing_free=yes" else "standing-equipment: a whole roster over real paths must pass free"
assert control.out contains "absent_path_refused=yes" else "standing-equipment: a rostered path absent from disk must be refused"
assert control.out contains "half_row_refused=yes" else "standing-equipment: a guard record with no path must be refused"
assert control.out contains "unrostered_run_refused=yes" else "standing-equipment: a run naming an unrostered guard must be refused"
assert control.out contains "recorded_red_refused=yes" else "standing-equipment: a recorded red verdict must be refused"
assert control.out contains "absent_card_free=yes" else "standing-equipment: a pier that has run nothing yet is honest, never broken"
assert control.out contains "never_run_counted=yes" else "standing-equipment: the never-run count must read what the card omits"
assert control.out contains "recorded_run_counted=yes" else "standing-equipment: a recorded run must lower the never-run count"
assert control.out contains "two_path_row_refused=yes" else "standing-equipment: a guard record carrying two paths must be refused"
assert control.out contains "known_tier_free=yes" else "standing-equipment: a roster naming a tier the runner knows must pass free"
assert control.out contains "lap_counted=yes" else "standing-equipment: the every-lap tier must be counted on its own line"
assert control.out contains "cadence_counted=yes" else "standing-equipment: the cadence tier must be counted on its own line"
assert control.out contains "cadence_never_run_counted=yes" else "standing-equipment: a cadence guard the card never names must be counted"
assert control.out contains "cadence_run_lowers_count=yes" else "standing-equipment: a recorded cadence run must lower that count"
assert control.out contains "tiered_card_free=yes" else "standing-equipment: a card carrying tiers must pass free"
assert control.out contains "unknown_tier_refused=yes" else "standing-equipment: a tier no runner honors must be refused"
assert control.out contains "unknown_tier_counted=yes" else "standing-equipment: an unknown tier must be counted as well as refused"
assert control.out contains "default_is_lap=yes" else "standing-equipment: a bare run must select the every-lap tier"
assert control.out contains "default_runs_lap_only=yes" else "standing-equipment: a bare run must leave the cadence tier alone"
assert control.out contains "default_card_lap_only=yes" else "standing-equipment: a bare run must record only what it ran"
assert control.out contains "no_git_reads_zero=yes" else "standing-equipment: a pen outside a repository must read zero staged rather than refuse"
assert control.out contains "tier_selects_one=yes" else "standing-equipment: --tier must select exactly that tier"
assert control.out contains "card_keeps_untouched=yes" else "standing-equipment: a pass must keep the card lines of guards it did not run"
assert control.out contains "all_runs_every_tier=yes" else "standing-equipment: --all must run every tier"
assert control.out contains "name_selects_any_tier=yes" else "standing-equipment: a guard named by hand runs whatever its tier"
assert control.out contains "name_runs_only_that_guard=yes" else "standing-equipment: a guard named by hand runs alone"
assert control.out contains "absent_path_reds_runner=yes" else "standing-equipment: a rostered path absent from disk must red the runner"

# The tree digest, both sides, on a real git repository the control builds and throws away. A lap
# that begins editing while the roster runs gets verdicts spread across two trees, which is REDS
# %221 -- so the runner measures the tree at the open and again at the close and says when it moved.
assert control.out contains "real_repo_digests=yes" else "standing-equipment: inside a repository the runner must digest the tree rather than read nogit"
assert control.out contains "still_tree_reads_no=yes" else "standing-equipment: a tree that stands still must read tree_moved=no"
assert control.out contains "still_tree_passes=yes" else "standing-equipment: a still tree with green guards must pass"
assert control.out contains "moved_tree_reads_yes=yes" else "standing-equipment: a tree changed under the run must read tree_moved=yes"
assert control.out contains "moved_tree_refuses=yes" else "standing-equipment: a moved tree must refuse under run_verdict=tree_moved"
assert control.out contains "moved_tree_keeps_lines=yes" else "standing-equipment: a moved tree must still print every guard line it learned"
assert control.out contains "red_outranks_moved=yes" else "standing-equipment: a guard red is the louder finding and keeps the verdict"

# The unclosed lap, both sides, on the same real repository. A reading on line one persuaded and the
# class fired again eleven hours later (REDS %223), so the runner refuses rather than reports -- and
# the refusal is proven against a clean cold open, which it must leave entirely alone.
assert control.out contains "clean_cold_reads_zero=yes" else "standing-equipment: a clean cold open must read zero staged"
assert control.out contains "clean_cold_passes=yes" else "standing-equipment: a clean cold open must run its guards and pass"
assert control.out contains "staged_cold_refuses=yes" else "standing-equipment: a full-roster pass over a dirty index must refuse under run_verdict=lap_unclosed"
assert control.out contains "staged_cold_refuses_early=yes" else "standing-equipment: the unclosed lap must refuse before the first guard runs"
assert control.out contains "staged_cold_skips_digest=yes" else "standing-equipment: a refused pass measured nothing, so it prints no tree digest"
assert control.out contains "staged_hot_passes=yes" else "standing-equipment: --hot must pass the same tree, since the staged paths are the round's own"
assert control.out contains "hot_still_reads_staged=yes" else "standing-equipment: --hot must still report the staged count it declines to refuse over"
assert control.out contains "staged_named_guard_free=yes" else "standing-equipment: a guard asked for by name is no lap open and runs free"
assert control.out contains "hot_composes_with_all=yes" else "standing-equipment: --hot must compose with --all"

assert control.out contains "control_verdict=ok" else "standing-equipment: the control must agree with itself"
say "RED and GREEN paths proven -- ten refusals bitten across forty-three behaviors, and the runner driven over a planted roster in and out of a real repository"

say "GREEN: standing-equipment -- the roster is a list a program reads, each row names its cadence, and running it writes down when."
